<title>USA: Apria, Vitas reach settlement.</title>
<headline>Apria, Vitas reach settlement.</headline>
<dateline>COSTA MESA, Calif. 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Apria Healthcare Group said it reached a settlement with Vitas healthcare Corp on the termination of a planned merger.</p>
<p>Under the terms, Apria paid $4 million to Vitas and each company released the other from any claims, liabilities and obligations in connection with the merger.</p>
<p>Apria expects total fourth quarter costs associated with the merger and its termination to be between $7 million and $10 million.</p>
<p>The two agreed to merge last June, but earlier this month Apria terminated the deal. Vitas then challenged Apria, saying it had no basis to unilaterally end the agreement.</p>
</text>
